    pr_ref:  # cfd9
    description: "WI-sudug taught us that test-fixture directories can contain build manifests that don't represent the project's real dependencies (detekt test fixtures had package.json with react). WI-duhom's parse_gradle_dependencies and parse_maven_dependencies in jvm_deps.py scan root + immediate subdirectories for build.gradle/build.gradle.kts/pom.xml. If a JVM project has testFixtures/build.gradle or similar at the first directory level, spurious dependencies could be promoted to tier 2 (INTERNAL_DEP) incorrectly.\n\nFix: mirror profile._find_manifest_files — use paths.is_test_file to skip manifest files inside test-fixture directories during the subdirectory scan. Only a few lines in jvm_deps.py._parse_gradle_file and ._parse_pom_file dispatch paths.\n\nLow priority because: (a) jvm_deps only scans depth-1, reducing exposure; (b) JVM test fixtures typically live at src/test/resources/ (depth-3, not scanned); (c) no bakeoff evidence yet that real Kotlin/Java projects are affected."  # cfd9
    fields: {}  # cfd9
